This doesn't work under symex-driven lazy loading because no entry-point function is given.

The pre-compiled class file was compiled from Groovy source using a
specific Groovy compiler version. It exercises JBMC's handling of
Groovy-specific bytecode patterns, particularly the Local Variable
Table format. The Groovy source is kept in src/main/groovy/ for
reference but is not used for compilation (different Groovy/JDK
versions produce different bytecode that may not match what JBMC
expects).
